%description:

Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass:vegas-dupack -- a fast retransmission of Vegas keeps 3/4 of the window plus three segments.

The claim (Tcp.ned): "the NED type of the algorithm of each connection"; the comment of
each algorithm module names its behavior. The claim of TcpVegas (its NED comment, after Linux): at a fast retransmission,
the window becomes 3/4 of the window in segments plus three segments.

The class vegas-dupack: TcpVegas::receivedDuplicateAck() retransmits the segment at the third
duplicate ACK, or earlier when its fine-grained timer has expired, and sets the window to
(w - w/4 + 3) segments, where w is min(cwnd, snd_wnd) in segments. This facet comes from the coverage gap loop: no test reached the code of this part. This test separates
"vegas" from the algorithms that halve the window and from TcpCubic.

Host under test: host1, with TcpVegas, without SACK (precondition); host1 sends 100000 bytes at
0.2 s, and the tap drops the 15th data segment the first time. Observation: level 2, the window
that host1 sets before the retransmission is (w - w/4 + 3) segments, where w is the window
just before it.

%# parameter: Tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# class: vegas-dupack
%# value: "TcpVegas"
%# key: *.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass
%# expected-result: PASS

%includes:
#include "ProtocolTest.h"

%global:

using namespace inet;
using namespace inet::protocoltest;

// The window before the last change and after it: the reduction of Vegas changes the window
// just before the retransmission.
static double windowBefore = 0, windowLast = 0;

static bool noteWindow(const MatchContext& context)
{
    windowBefore = windowLast;
    windowLast = context.event.value;
    return true;
}

Define_ProtocolTestProgram()
{
    return ProtocolTest("TcpAlgorithmClassVegasDupack")
        .intercept(tap("tap").from("host1").filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && ipv4.totalLengthField > 100B").nth(1).drop()
                     .describe("the 15th data segment of host1, the first time"))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
             .filterPacket("tcp.synBit == true && tcp.ackBit == false")
             .capture("isn", "tcp.sequenceNo")
             .describe("the SYN of host1")
             .within(0.5))
        .meanwhile(anyNumberOfTimes(on("host1.tcp").signal("cwnd")
                                        .filterEvent(noteWindow)
                                        .within(4.0)))
        .once(on("host1.tcp").signal("packetSentToLower")
                  .filterPacket("tcp.sequenceNo == {isn} + 1 + 14 * 1448 && pk.dataLength > tcp.headerLength")
                  .nth(2)
                  .assertEvent([](const MatchContext& context) {
                      double before = windowBefore, last = windowLast;
                      double mss = 1460; // snd_mss: the MSS of the handshake
                      double w = std::floor(before / mss);
                      return std::fabs(last - (w - std::floor(w / 4) + 3) * mss) < 1;
                  })
                  .describe("the retransmission of the 15th segment")
                  .within(2.0));
}

%activity:
EV << "TcpAlgorithmClassVegasDupack compiled\n";

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
*.host1.tcp.tcpAlgorithmClass = "TcpVegas"    # the parameter under test
*.linkDelay = 10ms
*.host1.app[0].sendBytes = 100000B
*.host1.tcp.sackSupport = false
include ../../parameter/ini/_bulk.ini
include ../../parameter/ini/_base.ini

%contains: stdout
PROTOCOLTEST TcpAlgorithmClassVegasDupack: PASS
